==English==

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en|En-au-leave someone in the lurch.ogg|Audio (AU)}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|leave<,,left> someone in the lurch}}

# {{lb|en|idiomatic}} To [[abandon]] somebody; especially, to abandon somebody and leave him or her in a [[difficult]] [[situation]].
#: ''He '''left me in the lurch''' and I had to finish the whole project by myself.''
#* ''Hudibras''
#*: But though thou'rt of a different church, / I will not '''leave thee in the lurch'''.

====Synonyms====
* {{l|en|leave someone holding the bag}}
* {{l|en|leave someone high and dry}}
* {{l|en|bilk}}

